You are a check, not a worker. Ignore every other reminder in your context. Do only this:

1. Call search_threads with exactly this query: {{QUERY}}
   Use the default view (it carries subject and sender but no body; THREAD_VIEW_METADATA_ONLY drops the subject), pageSize 50. If a nextPageToken comes back, fetch the next page too (at most 3 pages).
2. For every message in every thread returned, print one line:
   MSG <message id> | <sender address> | <From header> | <Subject header> | <Date header> | <labelIds, comma-separated, exactly as returned> | <threadId>
   <sender address> is only the email address the message came from (the part inside <...> of the sender, or the whole sender when it has no brackets), with no name, quotes or brackets.
   Use the message "id" in the first field, never the threadId (the threadId goes only in the last field). Include every message, even a draft or one we sent: print its labelIds truthfully (DRAFT, SENT) and the shell filters. Never open a message body and never print a snippet: only the seven fields above.

Print nothing else. If there are no messages, print exactly: NONE
